    "hash": "f986f86184fb420316e1eba6c5571556b29d8faa054b1a7a63bc47ea76b3f33d",
    "summary_one_sentence": "When mistreated farm animals overthrow their human master to build an egalitarian society, the power-hungry pigs gradually subvert the revolution into an even harsher totalitarian regime.",
    "summary_short": "Neglected and mistreated by their farmer, the animals of Manor Farm revolt and establish a self-governed society founded on the principle of complete equality among all creatures. However, as the pigs step into leadership roles, personal ambitions and rivalries quickly undermine the ideals of the revolution. Propaganda, censorship, and fear tactics are weaponized to suppress opposition and consolidate absolute authority. Ultimately, the new regime becomes indistinguishable from the oppressive human rule they fought so hard to overthrow.",
    "summary_long": "Driven to rebellion by the neglect and cruelty of Farmer Jones, the livestock of Manor Farm successfully drive him away and rename their home Animal Farm. Under the guidance of two prominent pigs, Snowball and Napoleon, the animals establish 'Animalism' and construct a set of commandments prioritizing animal equality and freedom. Initial productivity and morale run high as the community works together to build a windmill and secure their future. Tensions soon arise between the visionary Snowball and the cunning Napoleon, culminating in Napoleon using a pack of vicious dogs to violently banish his rival. With Snowball gone, Napoleon assumes total control, scapegoating his former ally for every misfortune and gradually altering the core commandments to suit his desires. As the workload increases and rations shrink for the working animals, the pigs grant themselves special privileges, human comforts, and absolute political power. Dissent is ruthlessly crushed through show trials and public executions, leaving the remaining animals intimidated and disillusioned. By the end, the original principles of the rebellion are erased, replaced by a single decree that 'some animals are more equal than others.'",
    "synopsis": "An animated allegory based on George Orwell's classic novel, 'Animal Farm' explores the promises and perils of popular revolution. Following a successful revolt against their human owner, a community of farm animals attempts to establish a utopian society based on equality and shared labor. However, as leadership consolidates among the farm's cunning pigs, noble ideals succumb to corruption, manipulation, and tyranny, offering a poignant look at how power can betray a movement's founding dreams.",
